FlashRAM saves for the test harness (hl64 M6, SaveGame): on top of ares-testharness.patch
as built on ares-host (the tree's testharness.cpp also carries the agent-mode shots).

 - testharness.cpp: with ARES_TEST_HARNESS set the cart's FlashRAM (the ROM header's save
   type flashram) starts erased, or from the raw 128 KB image ARES_FLASH_IN names, never from
   a <rom>.flash a run left beside the ROM; the guest's exit through the harness device
   writes the chip image to ARES_FLASH_OUT (it ends in _Exit, which skips ares' own
   Cartridge::save / emulator save: those only run at unload and every 30 s).
 - flash.cpp: the sector erase (0x4b page, 0x78 / execute) cleared 128 bytes, one page;
   the chip erases the whole 16 KB sector the page lies in.
Apply with: patch -p1 -d <ares source> < test/ares-flash.patch (test/run/ares.sh ARES_FLASH_*).

diff --git a/ares/n64/cartridge/flash.cpp b/ares/n64/cartridge/flash.cpp
--- a/ares/n64/cartridge/flash.cpp
+++ b/ares/n64/cartridge/flash.cpp
@@ -79,8 +79,11 @@
 
   case 0xd2:  //execute
     if(mode == Mode::Erase) {
-      for(u32 index = 0; index < 128; index += 2) {
-        Memory::Writable::write<Half>(offset + index, 0xffff);
+      //the chip erases a whole sector (128 pages of 128 bytes), not just the page
+      //named by the erase command
+      u32 sector = offset & ~(16_KiB - 1);
+      for(u32 index = 0; index < 16_KiB; index += 2) {
+        Memory::Writable::write<Half>(sector + index, 0xffff);
       }
     }
     if(mode == Mode::Write) {
